in @code

in @code/metalogue

in @code/metalogue/materialize

in @code/rust

in @prism

in @glass

in @meta

in @nl

# @code/rust/materialize — the Rust altitude's recognitive turn
# realisation.
#
# The metalogue-turn-pair recognition (2026-06-10, Alex → Mara via
# Reed): `@code/metalogue` declares the substrate-pull-correct
# ground for the AST altitude's metalogue. The shim direction
# (substrate utters → species emits) is realised PER-SPECIES at
# `@code/X/macro` shards (cf. `shards/code/rust/macro.mirror`).
# The recognitive direction (species utters → substrate
# recognises) is realised PER-SPECIES at `@code/X/materialize`
# shards — this file is the Rust-altitude binding.
#
# Why under `@code/rust` (not a new `@code/materialize` family or
# the prior `@mirror/realisation` home): per
# docs/specs/code-metalogue-surface.md §2 substrate-pull check,
# `@code/X` species carry per-language altitude grammars. The
# metalogue/materialize recognition sub-prism IS-A part of the
# language altitude (the way `@code/rust/macro` IS-A part of
# `@code/rust`, the way `@code/rust/cargo` IS-A part of
# `@code/rust`), not a sibling family. The classifier's INPUT is
# a `code/rust.ast`; the home pulls to the species altitude. Path-
# namespace property per
# [[architecture-shards-as-substrate-source]]: this file at
# `shards/code/rust/materialize.mirror` declares
# `@code/rust/materialize`. The path IS the declaration.
#
# === Inheritance from @code/metalogue/materialize ===
#
# The recognitive turn's contract (`classify` /
# `is_materialisable` / `target_altitude` action signatures, the
# `materialised_file` + `partition` carriers, the four laws) is
# declared ONCE at `shards/code/metalogue/materialize.mirror`.
# This shard inherits via `in @code/metalogue/materialize` per
# [[architecture-prism-as-trait-as-everything]]'s `<=` mechanism
# (`in @X` is the canonical import-and-inherit form). The action
# signatures below specialise the ground's parametric
# `declaration` carrier to a Rust-AST-parsed declaration; the
# laws come for free from the ground's `requires` clauses.
#
# === The 30th-instance training set, lifted ===
#
# Per the prior `shards/mirror/realisation.mirror` §"The training
# set" (now retired; the narrative lifts to the new home with
# minor edits to reflect the per-species binding):
#
# The 29 substrate-pull recognitions logged through 2026-06-08 in
# `roadmap/2026-06-08-rug-pull.md` §5 are the labelled (Rust-code-
# shape, substrate-altitude) pairs the per-species body's match
# table walks. Each row is one `classify()` training example for
# the Rust-altitude binding:
#
#   #16 lift (foundational, not zoom)               -> @prism
#   #18 eigensheaf (spectral decomposition)         -> @epistemologic/math/sheaf_laplacian
#   #19 five operations are Hodge primitives        -> @prism
#   #20 eigenspace (composition foundation)         -> @mirror/spectral/composition
#   #21 prophecy (derive fractures from topology)   -> @kintsugi/fracture/predicate
#   #22 score family root                            -> @mirror/spectral/score
#   #23 glass IS lens (four names, one primitive)    -> @mirror/lens + @mirror/loss
#   #24 oscillate_witness (next-oscillation)         -> @kintsugi/oscillate
#   #25 morphism_context (per-candidate slice)       -> @kintsugi/morphism
#   #26 shift(oid, T) typed-capability primitive     -> @mirror/spectral/portal
#   #27 template render (one operation, many uses)   -> @code/mirror
#   #28 "path was already half-built" (json lift)    -> @mirror/data
#   #29 "presence IS the signal" (SCM_RIGHTS)        -> @mirror/spectral/portal
#
# The discriminator's body (when it lands; T22 MVP at
# `bootstrap/src/realisation.rs` is the current boundary-Rust
# realisation, will lift to substrate-source through
# kintsugi-on-Rust when the consumer pulls) reads the
# `code/rust.ast` and walks the family roster: does this file's
# structural shape match `@mirror/lens`'s family? `@mirror/loss`'s?
# `@code/mirror`'s? The 29 prior recognitions teach the
# discriminator what "shape-match" means at each altitude.
#
# === The carrier vs the verdict (two surfaces) ===
#
# Per the ground's §"The carrier vs the verdict": the full
# `materialised_file` record is consumed by cross-wall kintsugi
# (T22+) to produce fracture proposals; the binary `is_materialisable`
# verdict is consumed by mosaic's `settle_on` and the audition
# altitude (`@mirror/spectral/audition`); the `target_altitude`
# projection is consumed by per-altitude fracture diffing. Three
# readers, three projections, one carrier — at this altitude the
# carrier IS the Rust-altitude binding of the recognitive verdict.
#
# === Five-op block ===
#
# Per the in-flight depth-2 recognition (#46 pending, glass for
# depth-≥1 declarations): this sub-prism uses `glass` since it is
# depth-2 (`@code/rust` is depth-1; `@code/rust/materialize` is
# depth-2). Cf. `shards/code/rust/macro.mirror`'s depth-2 `prism`
# declaration that the sweep will lift; this new shard uses the
# new vocabulary from birth.
glass @code/rust/materialize {
  focus materialize
  project materialize
  split materialize
  shift materialize
  settle materialize
}

# === Rust-altitude binding ===
#
# The three action signatures from `@code/metalogue/materialize`
# (universal contract) bind here to `code/rust.ast` as the
# species AST type. The contract and laws inherit from the ground
# via `in @code/metalogue/materialize`; this shard's job is the
# per-altitude binding plus the realisation cascade.
#
# Per [[feedback-craft-not-deliver]]: bodies are `\` until a
# consumer-pull tick. The boundary-Rust realisation at
# `bootstrap/src/realisation.rs` (T22 MVP, the hardcoded
# basename match table) IS the current consumer; that file
# lifts to substrate-source when the discriminator's body
# discharges through kintsugi-on-Rust at T22+.

# `classify(d) -> materialised_file` — the recognitive primitive
# for Rust forms. Reads a `code/rust.ast`-parsed declaration;
# emits the full materialised_file record (path / partition /
# target / verdict). Body discharges by walking the AST against
# the family roster (@io, @code/mirror, @mirror/lens,
# @mirror/loss, @mirror/data, @mirror/spectral,
# @epistemologic/math/*) and pattern-matching the file's
# structural shape against each altitude's declared grammar. The
# 29 substrate-pull recognitions are the training set.
classify(d: declaration) -> materialised_file { \ }

# `is_materialisable(d) -> verdict` — the binary projection at
# the Rust altitude. Reads `classify(d).verdict` projected
# through the partition; clear when materialisable at substrate
# OR clear-permanent-@io; opaque when mixed.
is_materialisable(d: declaration) -> verdict { \ }

# `target_altitude(d) -> ref` — the targeting projection at the
# Rust altitude. Reads `classify(d).target`; consumed directly
# by cross-wall kintsugi to produce the first fracture proposal
# against the target altitude's grammar.
target_altitude(d: declaration) -> ref { \ }

# === Citations + cascade context ===
#
# The Rust-altitude binding inherits all four laws (round-trip,
# OID-functionality, type-soundness, substrate-pull preservation)
# from `@code/metalogue/materialize` via the `<=` mechanism. No
# additional `requires` clauses are declared here; the obligations
# are universal across every species realisation.
#
# Spec context: docs/specs/code-metalogue-surface.md (the @code/
#               metalogue spec; the per-species realisation
#               matrix at §11 lifts to include both directions —
#               shim at @code/X/macro, materialize at
#               @code/X/materialize),
#               docs/insights/2026-06-09-mirror-as-content-
#               addressed-build-system.md (the adjunction
#               declaration ↔ realisation lift at the species
#               altitude),
#               docs/insights/2026-06-10-bateson-form-behaviour-
#               as-substrates-first-distinction.md (the form/
#               substance partition; the discriminator lives on
#               the form side at every altitude it operates).
# Substrate decisions: [[architecture-shards-as-substrate-source]],
#                      [[architecture-prism-as-trait-as-everything]],
#                      [[architecture-lift-as-load-bearing]],
#                      [[feedback-substrate-already-had-the-word]],
#                      [[feedback-substrate-pull]],
#                      [[feedback-craft-not-deliver]].
# Related shards: code/metalogue.mirror (the universal AST-altitude
#                  ground for the metalogue; the shim direction's
#                  contract),
#                 code/metalogue/materialize.mirror (the
#                  recognitive direction's ground; this shard's
#                  parametric parent),
#                 code/rust.mirror (the Rust altitude the
#                  sub-prism specialises),
#                 code/rust/macro.mirror (the shim direction at
#                  the Rust altitude; the sibling sub-prism that
#                  pairs with this shard at the metalogue's
#                  turn-pair),
#                 mirror/realisation.mirror (RETIRED — the prior
#                  home of the recognitive direction; one-tick
#                  deprecation pointer pending cleanup tick).
# Path-namespace property: this file at
# `shards/code/rust/materialize.mirror` declares
# `@code/rust/materialize` per
# `@epistemologic/property/path_matches_namespace`.

out @code/rust/materialize
out classify
out is_materialisable
out target_altitude
